                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238712050",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198118439987",
                            "num_reviews": 23,
                            "playtime_forever": 775,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 130,
                            "playtime_at_review": 702,
                            "last_played": 1793476825
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of my all-time favorite VR games, now even more so with a long-awaited update.\n\nAs basic and overdone of a concept as it seems (a standing wave shooter), Holopoint has always felt unique to the me in the VR industry because of its satisfying bow physics, interesting wave mechanics (having to shoot projectiles out of the sky and then dodging them when they come charging at you). Yet for nearly a decade I've been lamenting its lack of updates- and honestly, it was showing its age.\n\nBut now! A visual upgrade, new waves, new enemies, new areas, new bows, all for free?! This update alone is unironically one of my most hyped releases of the past 5 years. It has cemented Holopoint for me as one of the GOATed VR experiences, in the same league as Ancient Dungeon.\n\nDo you want to feel like some epic fantasy demigod slaughtering samurai by the dozens? Then this is the game for you. Dear developer: if you're reading this, my sincerest thanks for the tenth anniversary update!\n\n(also, though it doesn't really count, it feels quite good to finally be ranked #1 in this game by sheer virtue of being one of the first to play the new update and the scores getting a reset)",
